hi there steve kaufman here  i'm back i'm back in vancouver after a  month  or more  uh and i want to talk about enjoying  language learning  and i'm going to talk about how it  affects me personally uh new year we're  thinking of new year's resolutions  uh i've always wanted to learn arabic  farsi turkish i kind of want to get into  that  you know middle east central asian part  of the world that i don't really know  much about and so i in fact i took with  me a book of uh you know how to learn  the arabic alphabet and stuff  and you know what i just haven't got the  motivation to be perfectly honest and  what's  the what is pulling me back is not my  lack of interest in those languages but  rather the fact that i want to enjoy now  this year the languages that i have  already learned because  you know my korean isn't where i wanted  to be obviously my polish isn't where i  want it to be i want to work on other  languages because i enjoy the languages  so  obviously that initial period when  you're breaking into a new language is a  lot of hard work  and  it's like you know initially planting  your garden but now i'm at the stage  where i want to enjoy  uh the fruits of my labor more so  i recently i've been doing more  ukrainian i had a couple of  conversations in ukrainian  i'm going to go back to my korean so  this year is going to be a year of  consolidation  and  arabic and farsi and  you know hindi or whatever is going to  have to wait until next year and we'll  see what happens next year but i think  it's very important unless you know you  have to learn the language for an exam  or you have to learn it for your work  but for many language learners and  certainly in my case i learn languages  for enjoyment and i love doing it so why  would i put pressure on myself when you  know that motivation motivation that  strong motivation  isn't there it will come and when i do  have that strong motivation i will claw  my way through the difficulties of the  arabic writing system and  dealing with a brand new language and  get it to a point where i can actually  start enjoying  uh learning it but i've done that now  for polish i've done it for ukrainian  i've done for korean and now i have the  opportunity to go in there and enjoy my  reading and listening and eventually  talking to people and watching movies  and stuff so this year i'm devoting to  enjoying the languages that i have  already  engaged with so that's my kind of new  year's position on languages for this  year thank you for listening bye for now
 

